{
    "name": "E2E Spotify - api call and no match",
    "description": "End-to-end test for the Spotify connector - calls the raw Web API through Make API Call and drives Find Tracks into its notFound branch.",
    "type": "automation",
    "notes": {
        "9d1e109e-a7b7-4b3e-8d98-3afdd31d19f0": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 400,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nNeither component needs seeded tenant data.\n\n* **Make API Call** does a `GET /me/playlists?limit=1`. It works on an account with **zero** playlists too — the assert checks the paging object's `limit`, which echoes the query parameter back, rather than any item. That is what proves the `parameters` input is actually applied.\n* **Find Tracks** is *deliberately* configured to find nothing: a gibberish `query` plus `minScore 1` means no candidate can clear the threshold, so the component emits on its **notFound** port. Do not \"fix\" the query or lower `minScore` — the assert is wired to `notFound`, and a successful match would stall the flow until the `AfterAll` timeout."
        }
    },
    "flow": {
